# Working notes and drafts kept beside the source but not part of it
*_NOTES.md
*_DRAFT.md

# Agent state written beside the source when memory_dir/projects_dir are left at
# their cwd-relative defaults: memory stores, the knowledge graph, spilled tool
# results, checkpoints. This was excluded via .git/info/exclude, which is local
# and does not travel — so a fresh clone would leave all of it untracked in the
# working tree, and one `git add -A` would publish a session's conversation.
/.darkcode/

# Working notes, drafts and comparison material kept beside the source but not
# part of it. These are untracked AND were not ignored, so a single `git add -A`
# would publish them — and some carry a vendor name in the filename, which this
# project deliberately keeps out of its history.
DARKCODE_VS_HERMES_AGENT.md
THESIS.md
HANDOFF_PROMPT.md
NEXT_SESSION_PROMPT.md
project_detail.md
detail_*.md
*_prompt.md
multi_debate.txt
/mywebssssite/

# Agent tooling scratch: editor state, nested worktrees, session logs. Same
# reasoning as /.darkcode/ above — these were excluded only through
# .git/info/exclude, which lives in one checkout and travels nowhere, so a
# fresh clone would leave the lot untracked and one blanket add would publish
# it. Nested worktrees under .claude/ have already cost this repository twice:
# they broke two boundary scanners and put 364,481 cross-worktree edges into
# the knowledge graph.
.claude/
.aider*
.cursor/

# Stray, unreferenced asset dir (the embedded web assets live in server/web/).
# Left untracked and unignored, so a blanket add would sweep it in.
/ui/html/
